-- title:
--   Chart rings are G-stable with invariants the lower chart ring
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $K_2$ and $K_1$ be fields carrying $R$-algebra structures, with $K_1$ a $K_2$-algebra in a way compatible with the $R$-structures (scalar tower $R \to K_2 \to K_1$), and let $G$ be a group acting on $K_1$ by ring automorphisms, the action commuting with the $K_2$-scalars, and such that every $G$-invariant element of $K_1$ lies in the image of $K_2 \to K_1$ (`Algebra.IsInvariant K₂ K₁ G`). Let $S_2 \subseteq K_2$ and $S_1 \subseteq K_1$ be sets with $S_1$ the image of $S_2$ under $K_2 \to K_1$. Write $A_2 :=$ `chartAlg R K₂ S₂` and $A_1 :=$ `chartAlg R K₁ S₁` for the $R$-subalgebras of elements integral over $R[S_2]$, respectively over $R[S_1]$, i.e. the integral closures of $\operatorname{Algebra.adjoin} R\,S_2$ in $K_2$ and of $\operatorname{Algebra.adjoin} R\,S_1$ in $K_1$. Finally let $\iota : A_2 \to A_1$ be an $R$-algebra homomorphism which on underlying elements is induced by $K_2 \to K_1$. The assertion is that there exists an action of $G$ on $A_1$ by ring automorphisms such that: the inclusion $A_1 \hookrightarrow K_1$ is $G$-equivariant; the action commutes with the $R$-scalars on $A_1$; for the $A_2$-algebra structure on $A_1$ given by $\iota$, the action commutes with the $A_2$-scalars and every $G$-invariant element of $A_1$ lies in the image of $\iota$; and, if $G$ acts faithfully on $K_1$ and $K_1$ is a fraction ring of $A_1$, then $G$ acts faithfully on $A_1$.
--
--   This is the statement that forming the integral closure of $R[S]$ inside a function field commutes with passing to invariants of a group of automorphisms: the chart rings of the two-chart integral model over $K_1$ are $G$-stable, with invariant subring the corresponding chart ring over the fixed field $K_2$. It is used to transport group actions to the chart algebras of the modular curve at full level, in particular in the analysis of minimal primes of the ideal generated by the $j$-invariant in the chart at infinity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_exists_mulSemiringAction_chartAlg_and_isInvariant_of_isInvariant.lean

